---
const faqs = [
  { question: "Do you post the videos and manage my social accounts?", answer: "The production service covers the agreed planning, filming and edited files. Publishing, account management and ads are additional services unless explicitly included in your proposal." },
  { question: "How many videos will I receive, and when?", answer: "The proposal specifies video quantity, lengths, formats, subtitles, first edit and delivery dates, and revision rounds. These depend on the brief, not a universal package." },
  {
    question: "How much does short-form video production cost in Dublin?",
    answer:
      "The cost depends on filming time, the number of videos, creative planning and whether you need ongoing support. Send a short brief and we will recommend a clear scope before preparing a tailored quote.",
  },
  {
    question: "Do I need to be on camera?",
    answer:
      "No. We can guide you through a relaxed talking-head format, or build videos around your work, products, customers, voiceover and natural B-roll. The right approach depends on what your audience needs to see and trust.",
  },
  {
    question: "How fast will I see results?",
    answer:
      "There is no reliable fixed timeline for organic results. Reach and enquiries depend on the audience, offer, publishing consistency and what viewers do next. We distinguish video delivery from business results; views alone are not evidence of new customers.",
  },
  {
    question: "Can you guarantee views or followers?",
    answer:
      "No — and be careful with anyone who says they can guarantee organic reach. Platforms control organic distribution. We agree the deliverables and review process in writing. Any reporting or ongoing campaign work must be included in that scope.",
  },
  {
    question: "What if I tried video before and it did not work?",
    answer:
      "A video can look good and still fail because the message, opening hook, offer or distribution was weak. We review the whole path from the first second of the video to the action a viewer should take, then fix the missing part.",
  },
  {
    question: "Do you provide short-form video production outside Dublin?",
    answer:
      "Yes. We serve Dublin and North Dublin, including Balbriggan, Swords and Malahide. Other Irish locations can be discussed, with travel confirmed in the quote.",
  },
  {
    question: "What is the minimum commitment?",
    answer:
      "Monthly packages have a three-month minimum. This gives us enough time to learn what your audience responds to, improve the approach and identify a useful performance trend. After that, the service continues monthly with 30 days’ notice.",
  },
];
---

<section class="sf-faq" id="short-form-faq" aria-labelledby="sf-faq-title">
  <header class="sf-section-head">
    <div class="sf-kicker">Straight answers</div>
    <h2 id="sf-faq-title">Short-Form Video Production FAQ</h2>
  </header>
  <div class="sf-faq__list">
    {faqs.map((faq, index) => (
      <details open={index === 0}>
        <summary>{faq.question}<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <p>{faq.answer}</p>
      </details>
    ))}
  </div>
</section>

<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  mainEntity: faqs.map((faq) => ({
    "@type": "Question",
    name: faq.question,
    acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: faq.answer },
  })),
})} />
